We need to refer to the pre-state: whether the element was in the deque before the operation. That's `\old(this.contains(o))`? The class has a `contains` method defined earlier: `public boolean contains(Object o) ;`. So we can use `\old(this.contains(o))`. The result is the return value `\result`. So the assertion: `\old(this.contains(o)) => \result`. Probably also need to consider that if element not in deque, result may be false (but not required). The comment only states implication: if element was in the deque before, then result is true.

Thus assert: `assert \old(this.contains(o)) => \result;`

